response:
A “loop” is a way of repeating a set of instructions a fixed number of times.  For example, in C, you can use a “for” loop to repeat a set of instructions N times.  Here’s an example:

for (int i = 0; i < N; i++) {
    doSomething();
}

Here “i” is a loop variable that's incremented each time the loop executes.  The loop will last from “i = 0” to “i < N”, which includes “i = 0”, so in practice it will execute N times.

